"The patient underwent a robot-assisted radical prostatectomy with a Gleason 4+3 (ISUP grade group 3) and pT3a stage, with positive surgical margins and lymphovascular invasion, but no lymph node metastasis documented. The absence of seminal vesicle invasion is a favorable finding. The preoperative PSA was elevated at 8.6. The documented absence of lymph node metastasis is a positive factor. Conversely, the positive surgical margins and the presence of lymphovascular invasion introduce risk factors. The biopsy findings, showing a cribriform pattern, are noted. Missing postoperative PSA measurements and follow-up data widen the uncertainty regarding the subsequent trajectory. Information regarding postoperative PSA levels and their trend is crucial for refining the prognosis. The current heuristic horizon suggests a potential recurrence window. The fixed estimated horizon is 37.25 months. This represents expected follow-up without an event, not a known recurrence date. The sensitivity range is 27.94–46.56 months; its coverage has not been validated."
